    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_Asset">Select package resource</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_AssetText">Read resource text</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImportAsset">Stage package resource</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_AssetID">Resource ID</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Asset">Resource</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_PortType_PatchAsset">Package resource</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_AssetHint">Use the resource ID from this composite's resource list. Reading or importing verifies its length and SHA-256.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_MissingPackage">This node requires a composite package resource scope. Open the composite editor or run the installed composite.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_MissingAsset">Connect a package resource before reading or importing it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_MissingWorkspace">Connect a patch workspace before importing a resource.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_Resources">Package resources</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_ResourceId">Resource ID (letters, digits, dots, underscores, hyphens)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_AddResource">Add file</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_RemoveResource">Remove selected</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_ExportBundle">Export resource bundle</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_ResourceBusy">Wait for the current operation to finish before editing resources.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_ResourceHelp">Use these IDs in Select package resource nodes. Removing a referenced resource causes execution to fail. Save or export to include changes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_DependencyUnavailable">Required package is unavailable or disabled: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_DependencyVersionMismatch">Package {0} has version {1}; required range is [{2}, {3}), where * means unbounded.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_PackageConflict">Cannot be enabled together with package: {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_RuntimeUnavailable">Package {0} was disabled, removed, updated or became unavailable. Refresh the composite before running it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_Requirements">Package dependencies and conflicts</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_DependencyHelp">Installed/enabled packages only; this does not apply prerequisite patches. One line: package.id minimum maximum. Use * for no bound; minimum is inclusive and maximum exclusive. Versions use major.minor.patch (e.g. 1.2.3). An ID alone accepts any version.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_Dependencies">Required packages</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_Conflicts">Conflicting packages (one ID per line)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_RequirementsInvalid">Invalid dependency/conflict declaration. Check IDs, duplicate entries, numeric version bounds and self-references.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Plugin_Version">Package version</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_Applicability">Check patch applicability</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Compatible">Compatible target</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_OriginalStateMatches">Complete original state matches</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_DesiredStateMatches">Complete desired state matches</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Applicability">Applicability</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ShouldApply">Should apply</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Applicability_Applicable">Ready to apply</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Applicability_AlreadyApplied">Already applied</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Applicability_NotApplicable">Not applicable</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Applicability_Conflict">Conflicting state</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ApplicabilityHint">Check the complete original and desired states. Connect Should apply to a branch condition and place mutations on its True flow. This query does not skip unconnected mutations. Matching both states or neither on a compatible target fails the run.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ApplicabilityConflict">The target matches both original and desired states, or neither complete state. Review the patch conditions before applying it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_PatchOutcome_NotApplicable">Patch not applicable; no changes applied</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_PatchOutcome_NoChanges">No file changes applied; review individual applicability results</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ApplyGate">Gate patch application</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Apply">Apply</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Skip">Skip</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ApplyGateHint">Connect changes to Apply and read-only follow-up to Skip. In this graph, every file-changing node must be reachable only through an Apply output. Gates inside loop/parallel bodies are not supported yet; place the gate before the controller.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_GateGraphLimit">A gated graph supports at most 1024 nodes and 4096 connections.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_GateFlowRequired">Connect control-flow outputs to control-flow inputs using valid node identities.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_GateNestedControl">An application gate cannot run inside a loop or parallel body yet. Place it before the controller.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_UnguardedMutation">The file-changing node '{0}' is not exclusively controlled by an Apply output. Connect its flow input to the application path and remove bypass/Skip paths. A composite must expose a flow input to be controlled from outside.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExecutionFlow">Execution flow</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_CompositeLimit">A patch run cannot invoke more than 4096 composite nodes.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_CompositeReportHint">Composite execution results are listed separately. Completed execution does not mean changes were published; check the overall publication result.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeStatus_Running">Executing</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeStatus_Succeeded">Execution completed (publication is reported separately)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeStatus_Failed">Execution failed</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeStatus_Cancelled">Execution cancelled</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_CompositeParent">Inside invocation #{0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_CompositeRoot">Root workflow invocation</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_None">Applicability not checked</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_Observed">Observed preflight states (including nested calls): {0}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_Applicable">Applicable</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_AlreadyApplied">Already applied</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_NotApplicable">Not applicable</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeApplicability_Conflict">Conflict</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_AttributionLimit">A patch run cannot record more than 100000 file/invocation associations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_StagedBy">Staged by: {0}. Later edits may replace earlier content; see the net change and publication result.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeSkip_Condition">Not invoked: condition selected another branch</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeSkip_UpstreamFailure">Not invoked: an upstream node failed</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_CompositeReportTruncated">The report reached its capacity; additional skipped composites are omitted.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeSkip_PreflightRejected">Not invoked: workflow preflight rejected execution</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_CompositeSkip_NotReached">Not invoked: workflow ended without reaching this composite</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_PartitionPath">Resolve partition file path</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Layout">Layout</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_PartitionPath">Partition-local path</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_PartitionDirectories">Workspace contains partition directories</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_PartitionRoot">Workspace is the selected partition root</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_SystemAsRoot">Workspace is a system-as-root image root</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_PartitionPathHint">Select the actual extracted layout explicitly. A leading / is relative to the declared partition. System-as-root maps only system paths below system/. This does not detect partition identity or open images. Exists includes staged changes; connect it to an assertion when the file is required.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidPartition">Select a supported Android filesystem partition.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidPartitionPath">Use a bounded partition-local path with / separators.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidPartitionLayout">Invalid partition layout; system-as-root accepts only the system partition.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_system">system</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_vendor">vendor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_product">product</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_system_ext">system_ext</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_odm">odm</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_vendor_dlkm">vendor_dlkm</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_odm_dlkm">odm_dlkm</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_system_dlkm">system_dlkm</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryFind">Find masked binary pattern</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FindMask">Find mask</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_StartOffset">Start offset</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_SearchLength">Search length</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Alignment">Alignment</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_SkipMatches">Skip matches</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Offsets">Offsets</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryFindHint">Enter hexadecimal byte pairs (up to 4096 bytes). Empty mask means FF for every byte; otherwise supply the same number of mask bytes. Matching compares masked bits and includes overlaps. Offset/length/alignment/skip use decimal integers; length -1 means to EOF. Alignment uses absolute file offsets. Expected matches is the exact remaining count after skip. No file is modified.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryReplace">Replace masked binary pattern</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ReplaceMask">Replacement mask</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryReplaceHint">Uses the binary search range, alignment, skip and exact count rules. Replacement and optional bit mask must match the find length; empty masks mean FF. Unselected replacement bits retain their original value. Overlapping replacement windows fail. Changes remain staged until the outer workflow succeeds; preview discards them. Use applicability checks to distinguish already-patched files.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryPreviewHint">Replacement windows in staging order (before → after), not the final net diff. File publication is reported separately.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BinaryPreviewRow">{0}, {1} bytes, {2}: {3} → {4} {5}</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_BytesTruncated">(first 64 bytes only)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_WindowsTruncated">Additional replacement windows are omitted.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FstabQuery">Query Android fstab</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FstabEdit">Edit Android fstab</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Field">Field</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_MountPoint">Mount point</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FileSystemFilter">Filesystem filter (optional)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FlagName">Flag name</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_BlockDevice">Block device</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_MountPoint">Mount point</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_FileSystem">Filesystem type</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_MountOptions">Mount options</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_FsMgrFlags">fs_mgr flags</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_SetFlag">Set flag</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_DeleteFlag">Delete flag</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FstabHint">Android five-column fstab only, not recovery or /proc/mounts dialects. Select literal mount point and optionally filesystem type; match count is exact. Set value replaces one field. Flag operations edit comma-separated mount options or fs_mgr flags; empty value creates a bare flag. The old-value guard checks the complete selected field. Spacing, comments and unedited content are preserved. This does not validate device-specific flag support or mountability.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_DeleteEntry">Delete selected entry lines</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FstabAdd">Add Android fstab entry</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_BlockDevice">Block device</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FileSystem">Filesystem type</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_MountOptions">Mount options</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FsMgrFlags">fs_mgr flags</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FstabAddHint">Appends five fields using the existing newline style. An identical mount-point/filesystem entry is unchanged; a duplicate or different entry with that pair is a conflict. Other filesystem candidates remain untouched. Count reports existing matches (zero for a new entry). Text is not published until connected to a write/stage node. Device-specific flags and mountability are not validated.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcQuery">Query Android init.rc</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcEdit">Edit Android init.rc</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_SectionKind">Section kind</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Selector">Section selector</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Directive">Directive name</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedSections">Expected section count</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Service">Service</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Action">Action</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Import">Import</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcHint">Select a service name, an exact action trigger expression, or an import path. Section and statement counts are exact. An empty directive queries the header. Editing replaces or deletes body statements only; replacement includes the same directive name and its arguments. Old-value checks compare the complete raw statement. Quotes, escapes and continuations follow Android init syntax. Imports and properties are not expanded. This does not validate device-specific commands, service options or bootability. Connect edited text to a stage/write node to publish.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcAdd">Add Android init.rc statement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Statement">Statement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_IdentityArguments">Identity argument count</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcAddHint">Append one statement to selected service/action bodies. Identity includes the directive and the specified number of leading arguments: zero for a unique service option, one for a setprop property key. Identical decoded tokens preserve the original; duplicate identities or different remaining arguments are conflicts. Other identities coexist. Count reports sections already containing the statement. New statements use four-space indentation and the document newline style. This does not validate command semantics or bootability.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcAddSection">Add Android init.rc section</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_SectionText">Complete section text</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcAddSectionHint">Supply exactly one complete service, action or import section. Identity is the service name, exact action trigger tokens or import path. An existing section with identical decoded header and ordered body tokens is unchanged; duplicate identities or different contents are conflicts. The fragment is appended verbatim, preserving its internal newlines and comments; required separator/end newlines follow the target document. Count is one for an existing equivalent section, zero when added. Imports are not expanded and runtime semantics are not validated. Connect to a stage/write node to publish.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcHeaderEdit">Edit Android init.rc header</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcHeaderHint">Select exactly one service, action or import. Supply its complete replacement header of the same kind, without body or trailing comment. Preserves the body, indentation and existing trailing comment. Optional old-value checks compare the complete raw header. A new identity conflicting with another section is rejected. Renaming does not update start/stop commands or other references; check those separately. Runtime command, trigger and path semantics are not validated. Publish using a stage/write node.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Placement">Insertion placement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_AnchorStatement">Complete anchor statement</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_End">End of section</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_BeforeAnchor">Before anchor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_AfterAnchor">After anchor</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcPlacementHint">End preserves the existing append behavior. Before/after requires exactly one body statement with matching decoded tokens in each selected section. Supply the full anchor without a trailing comment. Continuations remain intact. Repeated application requires the existing statement to be the adjacent body statement on the selected side, ignoring comment-only/blank lines; a different position is a conflict.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcArgumentEdit">Edit Android init.rc argument</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ArgumentIndex">Argument index</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcArgumentHint">Zero-based argument index excludes the directive: setprop key value uses index 1 for value; service name executable uses index 1 for executable. Empty directive selects a single header. Value and expected old value are decoded text, not quoted init syntax; escaping is generated automatically. Existing arguments only; unrelated spacing, quotes, comments and tokens are preserved. Header identity conflicts are rejected; references are not rewritten. Runtime semantics are not validated. Publish using a stage/write node.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcReferences">Check init service references</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExternalServices">External service names</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ReferencesValid">Inspected references resolved</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Services">Known services</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_MissingServices">Missing services</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_DynamicReferences">Dynamic references</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_InvalidReferences">Malformed reference commands</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_AmbiguousServices">Ambiguous service declarations</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InitRcReferencesHint">Checks start, stop, restart, enable and exec_start in actions and service onrestart commands. External service names are caller-declared, one literal name per line; imports are not read. Property-dependent arguments remain unresolved. Duplicate local service names are ambiguous, including override cases whose load order is unknown. The boolean covers only these named references, not full init syntax, other commands, interfaces, classes or bootability. Count is inspected commands. Connect the boolean to Assert to block publication on unresolved references.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigQuery">Query UotanStudio fs_config</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigEdit">Edit UotanStudio fs_config</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ImagePath">Image path</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_UID">UID</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_GID">GID</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedUID">Expected UID</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedGID">Expected GID</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedMode">Expected permission mode</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigHint">Edits the space-delimited metadata dialect consumed by UotanStudio builders. UID/GID are unsigned decimal; modes are decimal (493) or zero-prefixed octal (0755), not unprefixed Android octal. Query returns zero-prefixed octal. Select exactly one literal image path; duplicates fail. Edits emit decimal permissions and retain trailing capability data without interpreting or applying it. This changes sidecar text, not host permissions or an image directly. Rebuild integration, SELinux labels and xattrs require their own operations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigAdd">Add UotanStudio fs_config entry</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigDelete">Delete UotanStudio fs_config entry</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FsConfigEntryHint">UotanStudio metadata dialect: decimal UID/GID, decimal or zero-prefixed octal permissions. Add appends a missing literal path with trailing capability placeholder 0; identical ownership/permissions preserve existing source and opaque capability data, while different values or duplicate paths conflict. Delete removes the whole entry line; absent entries are unchanged unless an old-value guard requires one. Count reports existing matches. Does not add/delete the actual file, apply capabilities or rebuild an image; compose those operations separately.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextQuery">Query file_contexts rule</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextEdit">Edit file_contexts label</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_PathExpression">Exact path expression</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_FileKind">File kind qualifier</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_Context">SELinux context</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Any">Unqualified rule</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Regular">Regular file</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Directory">Directory</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Symlink">Symbolic link</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Block">Block device</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Character">Character device</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Pipe">Named pipe</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_Socket">Socket</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextHint">Select one text rule by its exact path-expression spelling and file-kind qualifier. Unqualified selects only a two-field rule, not every kind. Regexes are not executed or converted to host paths. Edit replaces only the context token, preserving order, spacing and full-line comments. Duplicate identities, malformed fields and old-value mismatches fail. Context shape checking is not loaded-policy validation; overlap/precedence, compiled contexts and actual image xattr publication remain separate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextAdd">Add file_contexts rule</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextDelete">Delete file_contexts rule</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_FileContextEntryHint">Identity is the exact path expression plus file-kind qualifier. Add appends a missing rule; an identical existing label is unchanged and a different label or duplicate identity conflicts. Delete removes the whole rule line; missing is unchanged unless an old-label guard requires it. Count reports existing matches. Other rules retain their order, but adding/removing rules can affect effective labels: regex overlap, precedence and loaded-policy validity are not checked. Does not modify image xattrs directly.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageReadText">Read text inside filesystem image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_EXT4">EXT4</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Choice_EROFS">EROFS</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageReadTextHint">Reads a literal regular file from a raw EXT4/EROFS image, including staged image replacements. Links, traversal, special files and files over 16 MiB are rejected; decoded text is limited to 4 Mi characters. Enumeration has entry/path budgets and supports cancellation. The full image hash is checked before/after reading and retained as a publication dependency. Hash output identifies the extracted file. Sparse/Super/Payload containers require separate extraction. This node reads only; image modification/rebuild is separate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageWriteText">Write text inside filesystem image</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ImageCapacity">Image capacity (bytes)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExtractionBudget">Extraction budget (bytes)</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidImageBytes">Image capacity and extraction budget must be positive decimal integer byte counts.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageCapacityHint">Enter the target partition capacity in bytes. It is required and is not inferred from the input image size.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageWriteTextHint">Replaces an existing regular file in a raw EXT4/EROFS image and stages a metadata-preserving rebuild. Expected hash optionally checks the old extracted file. Identical encoded bytes skip rebuilding. Capacity is required; extraction budget checks declared sizes. Preview discards the result; publication occurs only after the entire graph succeeds. Each changed write rebuilds the image. Links, new files, Sparse containers, AVB/signature updates and device validation are separate operations.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageCollectText">Collect image text edit</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageApplyTexts">Apply image text edits</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ImageEdits">Image edits</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_PortType_ImageEdits">Image edits</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageEditsRequired">Connect an image edit collection before applying it.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageBatchHint">Chain collection nodes through Image edits; leave the first collection input unconnected. Each adds one distinct existing file without modifying the image. Limits: 256 files, 4 Mi characters per text and 16 Mi characters total. Apply validates all old hashes, rebuilds once and stages one image; preview discards it. Capacity is required. Collections are immutable so branches do not alter each other.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageReadAttributes">Read image file attributes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageSetAttributes">Set image file attributes</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidImageAttributes">UID/GID must be unsigned decimal integers; permission mode must contain three or four octal digits.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageAttributesHint">Reads or changes actual inode UID/GID and permissions in raw EXT4/EROFS, including root (/), without following links. UID/GID use unsigned decimal; mode uses three or four octal digits (644, 0755, 4755). Query returns four digits. Set retains file type, optionally checks old attributes and stages a capacity-limited rebuild. Identical attributes skip rebuilding. Hardlink aliases share changes; access ACL owner/mask-or-group/other permissions follow chmod rules while named entries remain intact. Malformed ACLs are rejected. ACL/capability/SELinux editing, AVB signing and device acceptance are separate.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageReadXattr">Read image extended attribute</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageReadXattrHint">Reads one raw extended attribute from the current EXT4/EROFS image, without following links. Data contains at most 64 KiB of original bytes. Exists distinguishes an empty value from a missing attribute. Names use printable ASCII with a namespace dot, up to 255 characters. The image remains a publication dependency. No text decoding, SELinux policy checks or capability/ACL interpretation is performed.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageSetXattr">Set image user attribute</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageDeleteXattr">Delete image user attribute</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_HexValue">Hex value</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedHexValue">Expected hex value</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Conn_ExpectedExists">Expected exists</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_InvalidXattrHex">Enter an even number of hexadecimal digits without spaces or prefixes, up to 64 KiB of bytes. Empty means an empty value.</x:String>
    <x:String x:Key="Node_Patch_ImageXattrEditHint">Sets or deletes a user.* extended attribute on an existing raw EXT4/EROFS inode. Hex values use paired digits without spaces or 0x; empty sets an existing empty value. Delete removes the attribute. Optional old-value checks use Expected exists to distinguish absence from empty. Hardlink aliases share edits. Capacity is required; preview discards the rebuilt image. Identical sets and absent deletes are unchanged. Security, ACL and trusted namespaces require separate operations.</x:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
